nginx-quic-client-silent.patch  (applies to nginx 1.31.8 as bundled in OpenResty 1.31.8.1,
after nginx-quic-exiting-worker.patch and nginx-quic-send-slice.patch)

HTTP/3: a connection whose client cannot be heard any more is closed, so that the browser
moves to HTTP/2 at once instead of waiting.

Problem (seen on production on 2026-11-11, on two phones on two mobile networks): while an
app of the phone uploads over TCP (the Nextcloud app), nothing the browser of the same
phone sends over UDP arrives at the server. Other TCP connections of the phone pass within
a second, UDP passes only in the second in which an upload chunk ends, about every 20 s;
what the server sends still reaches the phone. Firefox keeps waiting on its HTTP/3
connection: the requests of the player hang, most are given up, and Firefox moved the
video to HTTP/2 by itself only after four minutes. There it played, during the upload.
Reproduced with Firefox ESR 153 in lab/browsers/run-blackhole.sh (UDP of
the browser's machine cut for 60 s, a 340 KB piece requested every 2 s):

    server as it was          30 s without an answer, then 15 requests fail, then HTTP/2
    server closes after 5 s   the 2 waiting requests are answered over HTTP/2 after
                              1.8 and 3.8 s, nothing fails

The reason for the 30 s: a client notices only by its own idle timeout that it is not
heard, and every packet the server sends (it repeats what is not acknowledged) starts that
timeout again.

Change: new directive

    quic_silent_timeout time;       context http, server; default 0 = off

read, like the other QUIC settings, from the default server of the listener. With a time
set, each connection is looked at when nothing has arrived from its client for half that
time:
 - nothing the server sent is waiting for an acknowledgement: the server asks (PING), so
   that there is something the client has to answer. At most 15 times in a row without a
   request of the client in between; a client that is merely idle is then left alone;
 - nothing has arrived for the whole time and two probe timeouts have passed without an
   acknowledgement: the connection is closed the way a reload closes it (GOAWAY and
   CONNECTION_CLOSE with H3_NO_ERROR). The browser repeats the requests that were waiting.
A client that answers notices nothing. Without the directive not one line of this runs.

Files: ngx_event_quic.h (the setting), ngx_http_v3_module.c (the directive),
ngx_event_quic_connection.h (state), ngx_event_quic.c (timer, close),
ngx_event_quic_streams.c (a request of the client starts the count of questions again).

